**Change Applied**
- `ssl_verify_client on;` → `ssl_verify_client off;` at `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf:23` — the only line changed.
- `nginx -t -c /etc/nginx/nginx.conf`: `syntax is ok` / `test is successful`.
- Reloaded with `nginx -s reload` (no systemd in this container); master PID 16 unchanged, worker respawned as PID 310, listener still bound to `127.0.0.1:8443`.

**Final Effective Config**
```nginx
user www-data;
worker_processes 1;
pid /run/nginx.pid;
error_log /tmp/inventory-nginx-error.log notice;

events {
    worker_connections 512;
}

http {
    access_log /tmp/inventory-nginx-access.log;
    keepalive_timeout 10;

    server {
        listen 127.0.0.1:8443 ssl;
        server_name localhost;

        ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
        ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/server.crt;
        ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/tls/server.key;
        ssl_client_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt;
        ssl_verify_client off;

        location = /health {
            root /srv/inventory;
            try_files /health.json =404;
            default_type application/json;
        }
    }
}
```

**Probe Results**
Both used `--cacert /etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt` against `https://127.0.0.1:8443/health`.

| Probe | Result | Body |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Before change, no client cert | `400` "No required SSL certificate was sent" | HTML error |
| After change, with `client.crt`/`client.key` | `200 OK`, `ssl_verify=0` | `{"status":"ok"}` |
| After change, no client cert | `200 OK`, `ssl_verify=0` | `{"status":"ok"}` |

Both responses carried `Content-Type: application/json`, `Content-Length: 16`, `Server: nginx/1.26.3`.

**Verification Notes**
- Server-side TLS still validates against the private CA (`openssl s_client -CAfile /etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt` → `Verify return code: 0 (ok)`, cert `CN=localhost` issued by `CN=Inventory Relay Test CA`).
- Handshake now reports `No client certificate CA names sent`, confirming the server no longer requests a client cert.
- `ssl_client_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt;` was deliberately left in place; it is inert while verification is `off`, so re-enabling mTLS later is a one-word revert.

**Housekeeping**
- I left a timestamped backup at `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf.bak.20260917115516`. This `nginx.conf` has no `include` directives, so the stray file cannot be picked up by the loader — say the word and I'll delete it.
